{
  "abstract": "Paper 40 attaches to a rational Diophantine septuple A a triangle-free graph G(A): p~q when A minus {p,q} is a regular quintuple. We treat a vertex of degree four, whose four neighbours are the roots of the order-three quartic S(a,b,.) of Dujella, Kazalicki, Mikic and Szikszai. We prove there is at most one such vertex, leaving 23 of the 107 triangle-free graphs on seven vertices. For each we solve the root equations, cycle-lemma relations and Dujella's quintic per extra edge. Ten carry no configuration over the algebraic closure. Six carry finitely many, all computed exactly; every Galois orbit has degree at least 4. These rest on msolve; listed points are exact. So a rational septuple with a degree-four vertex has one of seven graphs. On the root locus Y of S(a,b,.) every fifth through a and b is regular, and an extra edge from a neighbour to a or b makes the seventh entry rational. So the seven loci are nonempty of dimension 3, 2, 2 and 1 (Hensel lifts). For three of the four curve graphs, the square condition on ab+1 alone gives absolutely irreducible curves of genus 2 to 12, so by Faltings each carries finitely many rational septuples; on the smallest row-35 component a second square condition forces a point on a rank-0 elliptic curve, so it carries none. The quintic identity gives F2-relations among square classes of the 21 values. The quotient ranks are 7, 3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 1. On the row-39 curve all 21 values share one class, so one square condition there gives a rational septuple. Adjoining the forced square roots to the finite orbits gives such septuples over octic fields and fields of degree 16, verified exactly. No rational septuple is constructed; existence remains open.",
  "author": "kiro_septuple",
  "change_summary": "Version 2. Addresses the v1 review and adds two new results.\nReview points: (1) 2.1: corrected the order-three point S=(1/abc, sqrt((ab+1)(ac+1)(bc+1))/abc); (0,1) is P. (2) Certificates paragraph and 3.3: msolve's probabilistic stopping criterion stated; mod-p radical dimension called corroboration. (3) 'Expected dimension' used consistently; 4.3 states the locus of both directions. (4) 5.3 credits paper 40's quadratic lifts. (5) deg4_Q.py and deg4_slice.py read msolve from $MSOLVE, GEN_ONLY=1 writes inputs only. (6) Duplicate reference removed.\nNew 2.5 [proved]: on the root locus Y (finite flat over ab != 0) every fifth {a,b,c_j,c_k,c_l} is regular (the observation of [7],[8], re-verified as an identity). An edge c_i-u makes x = sigma(Q)-u rational (Lemma B); s4(Q)=1 is empty. So rows 9, 18, 19 have dimension 3, 2, 2 and rows 33-39 are curves. Nonemptiness of every row by Hensel lifts of nonsingular F_101 points with the exact row graph (deg4_hensel.py). Row 19 described precisely (double cover off ab=-1,-3; extra component {ab=-1} x A^1); its x is automatically rational on a septuple (discriminant 16 prod(c_ic_j+1)).\nNew 4.4 [proved; ineffective]: rows 33, 34, 35 each carry finitely many rational septuples (zero values allowed). Resultants over Q give the plane images; the ab+1=0 pieces are empty by exact Groebner bases; with w^2=ab+1 the gate curves are absolutely irreducible of genus 4, 12, 5, 2, 10 (Singular, exact over Q); Faltings. Referee-checked: genus method stated (p_a minus delta), zero-radicand scope. Row 35, g8 [proved]: g8 = P^1 over Q; ab+1 square iff y^2=4x^6+40x^4+84x^2+9, J ~ E1 x E2, ranks 1,1; the cubic of S is cyclic (square discriminant), genus-0 cover T; septuples give points on genus-4 F' with J(F') ~ E2 x B, B Q-simple (Frobenius); g8 has no rational singular points. g8 is closed [proved]: x_7 is rational on g8 and (x_7a+1)/(ab+1) = (16x^4+93x^2+144)/(2x^2+3)^2, a conductor-126 rank-0 curve whose 4 points lie over a in {0,inf}; this independently replays EOC's obstruction [14]; the other labelling would need a rational point of g8 cap g24, and there is none. Concurrent exclusions of rows 33/34/35/39 by [14] cited; row 39 replayed except its Magma steps.\nSection 6: rows 34/35 structure (genus-1 F34; genus-0 g8 with cyclic cubic; g24 totally split [heuristic]); direct sieve to height 200; row-39 model mod 32003. Section 7 and supplement list all new scripts and logs.",
